{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Say.</b> Some say it is praise, like אֶת־יי׳ הֶאֱמַרְתָּ (Deuteronomy 26:17), but it seems to me that it is from the language of saying, in heart and in mouth:" "<b>They shall eat.</b> All the righteous, and it is a compressed expression, and the meaning is that you should not think that one righteous person alone shall eat the fruit of his deeds, and the meaning of this verse is joined to 'woe to their soul':"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Resolved יי' as YHWH per divine-name rules; the quoted form reflects a standard abbreviation of the Tetragrammaton."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:48.223272916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}